# Development snapshot: no release or DOI has been published.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file. Please also cite the original model source listed under `references`."
title: "fair-hunter-prey-simulation: a reference repository structure, git workflow, and data-handling convention for FAIR system dynamics models"
abstract: >-
  This repository publishes a shared scientific specification with Vensim
  and Stella Architect implementations and open Python inspection and PySD execution. It defines a directory layout that
  separates model structure from parameter values from simulation results, a
  git workflow in which the commit history documents the modelling process
  step by step, and conventions for handling parameters, lookup functions,
  scenarios, and reference time series as external, citable files rather than
  as values hidden inside a model file. The accompanying commit history and
  documentation address practical problems of version-controlling system
  dynamics models. The Kaibab Plateau deer-forage-predator
  model, published as Exhibit 4.11 of the open textbook "System Dynamics
  Learning Guide", serves as an example.
type: software
